Rule 1 (tensor-tensor inputs must be broadcastable across all dimensions; prevents size-mismatch error)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1
>>
Rule 2 (out must have the broadcasted shape of input and other for tensor-tensor mul)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ( (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_2, i)) ∨ (shape(v_2, i) = 1 ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)) )
>>
Rule 3 (matching dtypes for tensor-tensor mul; prevents unsafe cast to out)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 4 (scalar-integer other: out matches input’s shape and dtype; prevents cast error)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : tensor} |= (v_2 = v_2) ∧ ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i) ∧ dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 5 (scalar-float other: input must be floating or complex; out matches input dtype and shape; prevents cast error)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float, v_3 : tensor} |= (v_2 = v_2) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10) ∧ dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1) ∧ ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)
>>
Rule 6 (when either input is floating or complex, out’s dtype must match one of the inputs; prevents “Float can’t be cast to Short”)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= if ( (dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10) ∨ (dtype_(v_2) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10) ) then (dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1) ∨ dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_2))
